Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Ravji Sutar and Shriji Maharaj Once, Shriji Maharaj asked Ravji Sutar, &ldquo;Well, Ravji Bhagat! Do you faithfully observe the vartamans (moral and spiritual vows) now?&rdquo;
Folding his hands with humility, Ravji replied, &ldquo;O Maharaj! Now that I have found a true guru, how could I ever violate the vows?&rdquo;
Maharaj asked inquisitively, &ldquo;Who is this guru that you have found?&rdquo;
Ravji replied, &ldquo;I have found my own wife as my guru!&rdquo;
Maharaj asked with a smile, &ldquo;How so?&rdquo;
Ravji narrated the incident, &ldquo;O Maharaj! When I once strayed under negative influences and abandoned Satsang, I told my wife, &lsquo;Come, let us now eat and drink whatever we please and enjoy worldly pleasures.&rsquo; My wife immediately responded with resolute firmness: &lsquo;You may eat whatever you wish, but I will never abandon Satsang! And if you ever touch meat or alcohol, I will end my life that very instant!&rsquo; Beholding her unshakeable steadfastness, I too was compelled to remain steadfast in Satsang. Therefore, she has truly become my guru!&rdquo;
Hearing this, Shriji Maharaj laughed heartily and remarked, &ldquo;Indeed, she has proven to be your guru! Someday We shall initiate you as a Paramhansa, and then you will never again be troubled by worldly memories.&rdquo;
Then Shriji Maharaj asked, &ldquo;Ravji Bhagat, when you formerly traveled in Satsang, how was your food arranged?&rdquo;
Ravji replied, &ldquo;In the morning, I enjoyed breakfast of jalebis, motichoor laddoos, rich milk, and pendas. At noon, I dined at the homes of devotees on sumptuous feasts comprising sweets, delicacies, cooked vegetables, and pickles. In the evening, I relished sweet milk with sugar and rice.&rdquo;
Maharaj smiled and remarked, &ldquo;Behold! Such was the divine joy and nourishment you enjoyed in Satsang, but the moment you stepped away from Satsang, even that was lost!&rdquo;
Maharaj expounded upon this at length. Shortly thereafter, Shriji Maharaj partook of His meal and retired to rest upon His cot.
