Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Chaturbhai Thakkar of Nanodaru and His Departure to Akshardham About one gau (approximately two miles) away from the village of Dev Dholera lies the village of Nanodaru. There lived a devoted spiritual aspirant named Thakkar Chaturbhai. Once, he fell ill. The following day, he said to his father, &ldquo;Shriji Maharaj granted me His divine darshan and promised, &lsquo;The day after tomorrow, We shall come to escort you to Akshardham. Therefore, invite the assembly of sadhus currently residing in Dev Dholera here.&rsquo;&rdquo;
Thereupon, his father sent a messenger to respectfully invite the sadhus. When the sadhus arrived, they were lovingly served a sanctified meal of malpuas. Later, when the sadhus were invited to the house, Chaturbhai spoke before them, &ldquo;Tomorrow, Maharaj will personally come to escort me to Akshardham. Therefore, I offer five hundred rupees as a devotional donation to the Dholka Mandir, and one thousand rupees belong to my wife.&rdquo; Saying this, he reverently offered dhotis to the sadhus, bowed at their lotus feet, and prayed, &ldquo;Please shower your divine grace upon me.&rdquo;
The sadhus then returned to the mandir. Chaturbhai had his cot placed inside a separate room and instructed his father and brother: &ldquo;Please do not allow any women to enter this room. Furthermore, after my departure, sponsor a sacred feast (rasoi) for the sadhus at the Dholka Mandir. And O respected father! Are you all pleased with this pious act of charity that I have performed?&rdquo; They all replied wholeheartedly, &ldquo;We are all deeply pleased.&rdquo; Afterwards, Chaturbhai had sweet shiro prepared, and all the family members sat together and partook of the prasad.
The next day, when Shriji Maharaj arrived in all His divine splendor to take him to Akshardham, everyone began singing sacred kirtans with great devotion. At that supreme moment, keeping his consciousness (vritti) steadfastly absorbed in the divine murti of Maharaj, Chaturbhai relinquished his mortal frame and ascended to the eternal Akshardham.
From Shri Hari Charitra Chintamani, Part 3/319&hellip; 🙏
