Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Bodhabhai Bharwad of Kanotar and His Departure to Akshardham In the village of Kanotar in the Bavla taluka of Ahmedabad district lived a shepherd (Bharwad) named Bodhabhai. Through the divine association and travels (vicharan) of the holy sadhus, he became an exceptionally devoted and staunch Satsangi. He held the esteemed position of village headman (patlai) in Kanotar. He was uncompromising in observing dharma and spiritual disciplines. At his home, he had employed a pious Brahmin cook who served meals to everyone from a respectful distance; such was his devotion to purity and righteousness. Bodhabhai engaged in ceaseless bhajan of Shri Hari and lived with unwavering adherence to spiritual vows (niyam), steadfast faith (nishchay), and loyalty to Satsang (paksha).
Once, his son Shardul developed a severe fever. During his illness, Shardul was blessed with the divine darshan of Shriji Maharaj. Shriji Maharaj said to him, &ldquo;Shardul, We have come to take you to Our eternal abode, Akshardham.&rdquo; Shardul then humbly addressed his father, &ldquo;Father, Shriji Maharaj along with all the holy saints has arrived to take me; please grant me your permission so that I may depart for Akshardham with Maharaj. After my departure, please sponsor a sacred meal (rasoi) for the sadhus at the Dholka Mandir.&rdquo;
Hearing this, Bodhabhai was filled with immense joy and said, &ldquo;Son, what could be more auspicious and glorious than Shriji Maharaj Himself coming to escort you? Do not attach your mind anywhere in this mortal world.&rdquo; With these words, his son Shardul instantly cast off his mortal frame made of the five elements and ascended to Akshardham with Maharaj.
About a year later, Bodhabhai developed a mild fever and his bodily weakness increased. At that time, Shriji Maharaj arrived in a divine chariot (rath) to escort him to Akshardham. On the outskirts of Kanotar, some local cowherds were grazing their cattle. Shriji Maharaj asked them, &ldquo;Which is the road to Kanotar? Please show Us the way.&rdquo; The cowherds inquired, &ldquo;What business do You have in Kanotar?&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj replied, &ldquo;Today We have come to take Bodha Bharwad of your village to Akshardham.&rdquo; Hearing this, one of the cowherds accompanied Shriji Maharaj for about one gaau (nearly three kilometers) to show the path and pointed, &ldquo;The village visible ahead is Kanotar.&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj then reached Bodhabhai&rsquo;s house in Kanotar, granted him divine darshan, and said, &ldquo;Come to Dham, We have arrived to take you.&rdquo;
Bodhabhai then gathered all his family members and relatives and said, &ldquo;Shriji Maharaj has arrived in person to take me. Therefore, all of you lovingly chant the divine name of Shri Swaminarayan (dhun) and plaster the floor with holy cow dung.&rdquo; The floor was sanctified with cow dung, upon which Bodhabhai sat comfortably while everyone chanted the holy dhun. Chanting the divine name alongside them, Bodhabhai peacefully left his mortal body, boarded the celestial chariot with Maharaj, and departed for Akshardham. The entire village and his family experienced the unquestionable conviction of Shri Hari&rsquo;s supreme divinity. Witnessing how Shri Hari personally arrives at the final moments to escort His beloved devotees, many villagers embraced Satsang and took refuge at the lotus feet of Bhagwan Swaminarayan.
— From Shri Haricharitrachintamani&hellip;
