Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Gopalanand Swami Appears as a Divine Prophet at Vadodara&rsquo;s Vadi Mandir, Samadhi of Local Muslims, and Miraculous Land Expansion At the Swaminarayan Vadi Mandir in the city of Vadodara, drainage outlets were installed near the ascetics&rsquo; bathing well to channel wastewater into disposal pits along the temple&rsquo;s rear wall. Directly behind this boundary wall lay a settlement of local Muslims. Witnessing the construction, they created a fierce altercation, hurled abuses at devotees, and rushed with deadly weapons to attack them!
The following day, prominent royal officials Narupant Nana and Bapu Saheb met with the residents to pacify them; however, the residents obstinately demanded: &ldquo;Pull back your temple wall and dig inside your grounds; this is public land and our alleyway will become obstructed!&rdquo; The dispute reached Maharaja Gaekwad&rsquo;s administration, which cautiously advised the ascetics to avoid communal tension by finding alternative arrangements.
Finding no alternative drainage route within the compound, Sadguru Gopalanand Swami opened the rear window and stepped into their courtyard. Five to seven prominent Muslim elders seated under a neem tree looked up; to their transcendental astonishment, they beheld Gopalanand Swami in the glorious, radiant form of a divine Prophet (Paigambar / celestial Angel)! Awe-stricken, they began reciting verses from the Holy Quran, bowed in deep humility, and exclaimed: &ldquo;O revered Hazrat! We shall faithfully abide by whatever you decree!&rdquo;
Gopalanand Swami proclaimed: &ldquo;Behold, tonight you shall be blessed with the divine vision of Khuda Himself, and that Supreme Lord is none other than Bhagwan Swaminarayan! I am merely His radiant angel-monk. Act according to His supreme divine commandments!&rdquo;
That very night, all of them were plunged into deep samadhi! In that transcendental vision, Bhagwan Swaminarayan manifested before them as the supreme divine Prophet, instructing: &ldquo;Never commit violence against any living creature; safeguard Our holy ascetics and devotees, and chant Our sacred name upon rosaries. Having received Our divine darshan, you shall never enter the gates of hell! This narrow alley of three cubits shall miraculously expand thirty cubits wide tonight, yet the neem tree and temple wall shall remain undisturbed. In ancient times, Lord Shree Krishna rested His chariot here after carrying away Queen Rukmini, sanctifying this earth! Forty years from now, a magnificent stone temple of Shree Laxminarayan Dev shall arise here. Furthermore, the four graves in this yard shall miraculously relocate to the cemetery outside Ganjkhana Gate tonight!&rdquo;
Awakening from samadhi, the residents were stunned to discover their courtyard miraculously broadened into an expansive open square, while the graves had completely vanished! Overwhelmed with devotional joy, they spontaneously chanted the holy name: &ldquo;Swaminarayan&hellip; Swaminarayan&hellip;!&rdquo;
The following morning, citizens across Vadodara flocked to witness the miraculous transformation. Those who had brandished weapons to kill the devotees laid down their arms, donned sacred rosaries, and became steadfast lifelong guardians of the Swaminarayan Satsang!
