रवजी तुरंत मंदिर पहुंचा और सद्गुरु गोपालानंद स्वामी के चरणों में साष्टांग दंडवत प्रणाम करने लगा। स्वामी ने उसे पहचानकर वात्सल्य से पूछा: &ldquo;क्यों रवजी भगत! सब कुशल तो है?&rdquo; रवजी ने हाथ जोड़कर कहा: &ldquo;स्वामी! मैं वही पापी रवजी हूं। आप जैसे परम संत को आघात पहुंचाने वाला संसारी जीव भला कुशल कैसे हो सकता है!&rdquo;
स्वामी ने पूछा: &ldquo;रवजी भगत, सुखी तो हो न?&rdquo; यह सुनते ही रवजी की आंखों से आंसुओं की धारा बह निकली। वह कुछ बोल न सका। तब परम दयालु गोपालानंद स्वामी ने धीरज बंधाया: &ldquo;रवजी भगत! जो भी कष्ट हो निःसंकोच कहो। हम संत श्रीजी महाराज से प्रार्थना करके तुम्हारा कष्ट अवश्य दूर करेंगे!&rdquo;
स्वामी की करुणा पाकर रवजी ने कहा: &ldquo;स्वामी! वर्षों पूर्व मेरे हाथ से आपको पत्थर लगा था&hellip;&rdquo; स्वामी हंसकर बोले: &ldquo;हां, वह तो हमें याद है! किंतु हम तो साधु हैं; क्षमा करना ही हमारा धर्म है। शिक्षापत्री में श्रीहरि की आज्ञा है कि कोई मारे तो भी उसका बुरा न चाहना। और उस पत्थर के बदले हमें आप जैसा प्रेमी सत्संगी मिला, इसका हमें आनंद है!&rdquo;
रवजी रोते हुए बोला: &ldquo;स्वामी! आप तो दया के सागर हैं, किंतु आप जैसे महापुरुष को पत्थर मारने के पाप से मेरा जीवन व्यर्थ हो गया है! विवाह के वर्षों बीत जाने पर भी मेरे कोई संतान नहीं है, मैं निःसंतान (बांझ) हूं! हे स्वामी! मुझ पर दया कर मुझे एक पुत्र प्रदान कीजिए!&rdquo;
रवजी भगत की दीन पुकार सुनकर सद्गुरु गोपालानंद स्वामी ने नेत्र बंद कर भगवान श्रीस्वामीनारायण का ध्यान धरा और रवजी के कल्याण हेतु प्रार्थना की। कुछ क्षण बाद स्वामी बोले: &ldquo;रवजी भगत! भगवान श्रीस्वामीनारायण आपकी इच्छा पूर्ण करेंगे, जाइए हमारा वचन है! श्रीहरि आपका कल्याण करेंगे।&rdquo;
स्वामी अगले दिन विचरण हेतु चले गए। किंतु स्वामी के पावन वरदान के प्रभाव से एक वर्ष के भीतर रवजी भगत के घर एक तेजस्वी पुत्र का जन्म हुआ! पूरे परिवार में आनंद छा गया। दो वर्ष पश्चात रवजी भगत अपनी पत्नी और पुत्र को बैलगाड़ी में बिठाकर गढ़पुर पहुंचे। गोपीनाथजी महाराज और अक्षर ओरडी के दर्शन कर गोपालानंद स्वामी के चरणों में बालक को रखा: &ldquo;स्वामी! आपकी दया से यह बालक जन्मा है, आप ही इस पर हाथ रखकर आशीर्वाद दीजिए और नामकरण कीजिए!&rdquo;
गोपालानंद स्वामी ने बालक को वर्तमान धारण कराकर नामकरण किया और उपदेश दिया: &ldquo;रवजी भगत! भगवान श्रीस्वामीनारायण ने आपकी मनोकामना पूर्ण की है; अब जीवन के समस्त कार्य करते हुए उन प्रभु को कभी विस्मृत मत करना!&rdquo; इस प्रकार महान संत की वास्तविक क्षमा और कृपा से पश्चातापी जीव का उद्धार होकर उसका जीवन धन्य हो जाता है।
Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Sadguru Gopalanand Swami&rsquo;s Forgiveness upon Ravji Koli of Kundani, True Repentance, and the Boon of a Son In the Jasdan taluka of the Panchal region lies a modest village named Kundani. One evening, a poor farmer named Ravji Koli returned home from his agricultural labour with his dilapidated bullock cart and lean oxen. As soon as he arrived, his wife greeted him with news: &ldquo;Listen! Holy Swaminarayan ascetics have arrived at our village temple today. Among them is the very saint who was once struck unconscious by a stone thrown from your hand! Go to the temple, seek his forgiveness, and beg for his blessings so that our past sins may be eradicated and our hardship removed!&rdquo;
The memory of that unfortunate incident flashed vividly before Ravji&rsquo;s mind. Years earlier, during a heated dispute with a local merchant, Ravji had hurled a stone in anger; the stone accidentally struck Sadguru Gopalanand Swami as he passed by, causing the great saint to collapse unconscious! True to the tenets of the Shikshapatri, which commands ascetics never to harbor ill-will even toward those who abuse or strike them, Swami had instantly forgiven Ravji without a trace of resentment. Overwhelmed by remorse, Ravji had embraced the Swaminarayan faith.
Ravji rushed to the temple and fell prostrate in humble dandvat pranam at Sadguru Gopalanand Swami&rsquo;s holy feet. Recognizing him instantly, Swami enquired with tender affection, &ldquo;Well, Ravji Bhagat! Are you well and at peace?&rdquo; Folding his hands, Ravji wept, &ldquo;Swami! I am that same unfortunate Ravji. How can a worldly creature who struck an exalted saint ever be truly at peace!&rdquo;
Swami asked gently, &ldquo;Ravji Bhagat, are you happy?&rdquo; Hearing Swami&rsquo;s compassionate tone, tears poured from Ravji&rsquo;s eyes like torrential monsoon rain, leaving him choked and speechless. The merciful Gopalanand Swami consoled him: &ldquo;Ravji Bhagat! Whatever sorrow burdens your heart, speak without hesitation. We sadhus shall pray to Shreeji Maharaj and dispel your misery!&rdquo;
Encouraged by Swami&rsquo;s boundless compassion, Ravji confessed, &ldquo;Swami! Years ago, my hand hurled that stone which injured you in the village bazaar&hellip;&rdquo; Swami smiled warmly and remarked, &ldquo;Yes, we remember that well! But we are sadhus; forgiveness is our intrinsic spiritual duty. In the Shikshapatri, Shreehari has commanded that even if someone strikes us, we must never wish ill upon them. Moreover, in exchange for that stone, we gained a sincere devotee like you, which brings us immense joy!&rdquo;
Ravji wept bitterly, &ldquo;Swami, you are an ocean of saintliness, but the sin of striking an exalted devotee of God has poisoned my existence! Years have passed since my marriage, yet I have no offspring; I remain childless! O merciful master, bless me with a son!&rdquo;
Moved by Ravji&rsquo;s heartfelt repentance, Sadguru Gopalanand Swami closed his eyes, meditated upon Bhagwan Swaminarayan, and prayed for the relief of Ravji&rsquo;s affliction. Opening his eyes, Swami declared: &ldquo;Ravji Bhagat! Bhagwan Swaminarayan will fulfill your aspiration; go, it is my promise! Shreehari shall bestow all auspiciousness upon you.&rdquo;
The next day, Swami proceeded on his spiritual itinerancy. Within one year, by the unfailing potency of Swami&rsquo;s divine boon, a radiant son was born into Ravji Bhagat&rsquo;s household, filling his home with festive celebration! Two years later, Ravji hitched his bullock cart and brought his wife and child to Gadhpur. After offering devout prayers to Gopinathji Maharaj and visiting the sacred Akshar Ordi, he placed the toddler at Gopalanand Swami&rsquo;s holy feet: &ldquo;Swami! By your grace this son was granted; kindly place your blessing hand upon him and bestow his name!&rdquo;
Gopalanand Swami initiated the child with the sacred vows of Satsang, named him, and imparted spiritual counsel: &ldquo;Ravji Bhagat! Bhagwan Swaminarayan has fulfilled your desire; now, while carrying out all worldly duties, never forget that Supreme Lord!&rdquo; Thus, through the sublime forgiveness and divine grace of an enlightened saint, a repentant soul&rsquo;s sins were dissolved, bestowing eternal spiritual auspiciousness.
