Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Ailing Sadhu in Fareni and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Divine Medicine Once, Shriji Maharaj was residing in the village of Fareni. There, a sadhu was gravely ill; his entire body had become severely swollen, and his inflamed gums covered his teeth. Witnessing his condition, Devanand Sanyasi approached Shriji Maharaj and asked, &ldquo;Maharaj, a sadhu is critically ill, and his ailment cannot be diagnosed. What medicine should we administer to him?&rdquo;
Maharaj replied, &ldquo;That sadhu does not belong to this universe. Therefore, feed him sour buttermilk and ghesh (a gruel cooked in buttermilk). Even if he asks for water to drink, give him buttermilk.&rdquo;
Devanand Sanyasi questioned, &ldquo;Maharaj, can buttermilk be given to someone whose body is afflicted with swelling?&rdquo;
Maharaj replied, &ldquo;Administer the medicine We have instructed. If it proves effective, well and good; otherwise, he will depart to Dham (Akshardham).&rdquo;
Thereafter, Devanand Swami went to the ailing sant. When he asked for food, Swami gave him ghesh prepared in buttermilk, and when he asked for water to drink, Swami gave him buttermilk again. Having partaken of this merely twice, all the swelling completely subsided, and the sadhu became completely healthy.
In this divine manner, Shriji Maharaj cured the sadhu of an incurable illness through His wondrous remedy.
