Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Khokhra River and Shriji Maharaj&rsquo;s Auspicious Muhurt Once, the Supreme Lord Shriji Maharaj, riding His beloved mare Manki and accompanied by staunch Kathi devotees including Sura Khachar and Somla Khachar, was travelling via the village of Samadhiyala. Near Sajdiyali, they halted on the banks of the Khokhra River to let the horses drink water and rest.
Meanwhile, a villager informed the local devout devotees, Kana Patel and Vasta Patel: &ldquo;Your Bhagwan Swaminarayan has arrived right here at the river near our village!&rdquo; Overjoyed upon hearing this auspicious news, both devotees came running in haste. With immense devotion, they offered prostrations (dandvat pranam) at Shriji Maharaj’s lotus feet and paid their humble respects. They fervently pleaded with Shri Hari to grace their home in the village. However, Shri Hari gently remarked, &ldquo;It will be late today, and We still have a long journey ahead. Let us sit together here on the soft riverbed for a little while.&rdquo; Everyone then sat comfortably in the sandy bed of the Khokhra River.
At that moment, Kana Patel folded his hands and prayed with utmost humility: &ldquo;O Maharaj! In our village, there is not a single family of a Brahmin priest or astrologer. Whenever we need to determine an auspicious time (muhurt) for farming or harnessing the ploughs for sowing crops (vavaniya), whom should we consult?&rdquo; Hearing his sincere concern, the benevolent Shri Hari smiled warmly and said, &ldquo;O Kana Bhagat! Whatever work you commence, chant the sacred divine name &lsquo;Swaminarayan&hellip; Swaminarayan&hellip;!&rsquo; with sincere devotion and begin your sowing. The remembrance of God&rsquo;s holy name is itself the greatest and most auspicious muhurt for you!&rdquo;
Kana Patel then inquired further: &ldquo;O Maharaj! When we construct a new home, how should we perform the house-warming ceremony (Vastu-pujan) and determine its auspicious timing?&rdquo;
Shri Hari showered His grace and revealed, &ldquo;In your new house, respectfully enshrine the sacred scripture Shikshapatri and light a sacred lamp before it. Then, let everyone sit together and sing the divine Swaminarayan&hellip; Swaminarayan&hellip; mahamantra. That devout worship is itself the supreme and most auspicious muhurt! We shall personally eradicate every obstacle and adversity from your life.&rdquo;
Both faithful satsangi brothers enshrined Shri Hari’s divine command (agna) in their hearts, holding it supreme throughout their entire lives.
