Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English Brahmanand Swami&rsquo;s Divine Conviction and Shriji Maharaj Once in Gadhpur, Shriji Maharaj was seated under the sacred Neem tree presiding over an assembly of holy souls. Eminent Nand-saints and paramhansas were seated before Him. Shri Hari was bestowing the bliss of His divine darshan upon all. After an enlightening session of spiritual questions and answers, Shri Hari said, &ldquo;Today, let everyone speak about their personal conviction (nishchay) regarding My divine swaroop.&rdquo; Shriji Maharaj addressed the realized paramhansas capable of granting samadhi, such as Swarupanand Swami, Vyapkanand Swami, and Shatanand Swami, but out of reverent humility, no one spoke.
Shriji Maharaj urged, &ldquo;Why is no one speaking? Whatever understanding resides in your heart, you must speak today!&rdquo; Then Sadguru Muktanand Swami submitted, &ldquo;O Maharaj! None of them will speak out of hesitation; please ask Brahmanand Swami.&rdquo;
Maharaj then called upon Sadguru Brahmanand Swami and said, &ldquo;Swami, speak of your conviction.&rdquo; Brahmanand Swami reverently said, &ldquo;Maharaj, in one of my own kirtans I have sung: &lsquo;Brahmānandnā Nāth tamāro mahimā jāṇe chhe moṭā gyānī re&rsquo; (&lsquo;O Lord of Brahmanand, only great enlightened souls can truly comprehend Your glory&rsquo;).&rdquo;
Maharaj smiled and replied, &ldquo;That is certainly true, but express the joy and conviction exactly as it lives within your heart.&rdquo;
Hearing these words from Maharaj, Brahmanand Swami spoke with divine grandeur: &ldquo;O Maharaj! When I was a small child, I contemplated that ordinary worldly children play with trivial toys, but I was not like them. Although having taken a human body I was considered a child, I decided that if I was to play, I should play with something truly grand. Thereupon, with a single divine attraction, I gathered into one hand the suns, moons, stars, fires, guardian deities (Lokpals), King Indra, Brahma, Vairat, Ishwars, Pradhan-Purush, and Mahapurush of infinite crores of universes, and played with them as my toys! Then, with another divine resolve (sankalpa), I recreated the Ishwars, jivas, and devas of each respective universe, and all cosmic activities across those realms continued uninterrupted. Then I reflected: &lsquo;This is merely cosmic play within my own divine nature; what true fulfillment is there in playing with this?&rsquo;
&lsquo;Now let me seek an even greater, boundless bliss!&rsquo; Saying this, I directed my vision toward the pure divine Self (Atman/Akshar). There, I experienced a realm supremely tranquil, cool, replete with infinite divine virtues, and unfathomable. As I sought to fathom its depth, no end could be found! Then I sought to know: &lsquo;Who is the ultimate Sovereign and Controller of this infinite bliss?&rsquo;
There, I beheld a vast, boundless divine assembly radiating the supreme form of Purushottam, and my heart was filled with boundless love. Then the thought arose: &lsquo;Who is supreme among all in this assembly?&rsquo; And there, O Maharaj, I beheld You seated supreme above all! Instantly, the profound conviction awoke within me: &lsquo;This Maharaj is eternally mine, and I belong to this Maharaj!&rsquo; When I tried to trace back to when this divine bond was formed, no beginning could ever be found—this bond is eternal (anadi)!&rdquo; Having expressed this, Brahmanand Swami humbly took his seat.
Shriji Maharaj then inquired with a smile, &ldquo;Swami, why did you stop speaking? Why not continue?&rdquo;
Brahmanand Swami replied with immense reverence and humility, &ldquo;O Maharaj! The conviction I have just spoken of was what I possessed when I was merely a small child. Now, I have grown up, embraced the life of a renunciant sadhu, enjoyed Your constant holy association, and served You personally. Therefore, my present conviction regarding Your divine supremacy is infinitely greater than that—it is utterly indescribable in words&hellip;!&rdquo;
From the life and teachings of Sadguru Brahmanand Swami&hellip; 🙏
