Goto Naviagation&#x1f447; English The Vairagi of Gondal and the Prophecy of Shriji Maharaj Once, Shri Hari graced the town of Gondal with His holy presence, accompanied by Sadguru Muktanand Swami, saints, and devotees. Shri Hari was camping in the Fulwadi garden situated on the eastern side of the town. Beneath the cool shade of a large tree, Ratna Bhagat and all the local devotees were seated in an assembly around Shri Hari.
At that time, a Vairagi named Devmukt arrived before Shri Hari, accompanied by a few prominent town merchants. Being proud, arrogant, and filled with spite, this Vairagi began uttering perverse remarks and behaving rudely. Seeing this, Shri Hari stopped conversing and became silent. After a brief pause, Shriji Maharaj subtly gestured to Muktanand Swami. Understanding the hint, Swami began speaking on the glory of Satsang and spiritual wisdom.
After listening for a short while, the Vairagi retorted, &ldquo;The words of this Sadhu Muktanand are straightforward and easy to understand, but the words of this Swaminarayan cannot be understood at all.&rdquo;
Upon this, Muktanand Swami replied, &ldquo;The divine words of Bhagwan Swaminarayan cannot be comprehended in a mere moment! All of us have renounced our homes, families, and worldly life, yet even we cannot fully fathom His divine words. The scriptures describe Him as &lsquo;Neti, Neti&rsquo; (not this, not that), and even the four Vedas cannot reach the depths of His greatness. How then can ordinary souls like us comprehend His profound wisdom&hellip;!&rdquo;
The Vairagi Devmukt then posed several questions to Muktanand Swami. Swami joyfully answered each query, resolving the thoughts and doubts in his mind. However, when Swami questioned him in return, the Vairagi began evading and could give no answer. Instead, out of frustration, he began blabbering maliciously, &ldquo;All of this is merely your hypocrisy, deception, and pretense! You are cheating the world.&rdquo;
Shriji Maharaj smiled gently and said, &ldquo;There is no end to the perversity of the jiva. Whether this is our hypocrisy or yours, within six months time will reveal the truth to everyone.&rdquo;
Hearing these words of Shri Hari and realizing their pride was wounded, the Vairagi Devmukt and his disciples promptly slipped away.
The following day, Shri Hari, Muktanand Swami, and the entire congregation departed from Gondal, traveling via Moka Khachar&rsquo;s Vankiya on their way to Gadhpur.
About six months later, that same Vairagi was caught red-handed in a burglary in the town. The royal guards apprehended him and presented him before the royal council, where the minister (Diwan) threw him into prison. His wicked deeds and hypocrisy were thus exposed to all the townspeople. Suffering the grave consequences of blaspheming against Supreme Lord Shri Hari, he met his demise while still in prison.
From Shri Hari Charitra Chintamani&hellip; 🙏
